From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Buildroot Board Support <buildroot@example.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: prepare shared USB controller for Wi-Fi host mode

The MangoPi R3 AIC8800D40 board uses the sole MUSB controller as a Linux
USB host for an internally connected Wi-Fi module.  U-Boot initially
probes the controller as a gadget for recovery features, but leaving it in
peripheral mode prevents the attached module from seeing the first host
connect event.

Hold the module's WIFI_EN signal low from board_init() so that it cannot
claim the shared bus while U-Boot is serving DFU or UMS.  Linux owns PE4
and enables the module only after switching MUSB to host mode.

Remove the active gadget device during the normal U-Boot-to-Linux handoff.
Interactive U-Boot DFU and UMS stay available until Linux is booted.

Signed-off-by: Buildroot Board Support <buildroot@example.com>
---
 board/sunxi/board.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/sunxi/board.c b/board/sunxi/board.c
index 83c58762f1..0a3cc08f76 100644
--- a/board/sunxi/board.c
+++ b/board/sunxi/board.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 
 #include <common.h>
 #include <dm.h>
+#include <dm/device-internal.h>
 #include <env.h>
 #include <hang.h>
 #include <image.h>
@@ -226,6 +227,20 @@
 
 	gd->bd->bi_boot_params = (PHYS_SDRAM_0 + 0x100);
 
+	/*
+	 * MUSB is a DFU/UMS gadget in U-Boot, while the internal AIC8800D40
+	 * is a USB device.  Keep the module disconnected until Linux switches
+	 * the controller to host mode and takes ownership of WIFI_EN.
+	 */
+	ret = gpio_request(SUNXI_GPE(4), "wifi-enable");
+	if (ret) {
+		printf("Failed to request WIFI_EN: %d\n", ret);
+	} else {
+		ret = gpio_direction_output(SUNXI_GPE(4), 0);
+		if (ret)
+			printf("Failed to disable Wi-Fi module: %d\n", ret);
+	}
+
 #if !defined(CONFIG_ARM64) && !defined(CONFIG_MACH_SUNIV)
 	asm volatile("mrc p15, 0, %0, c0, c1, 1" : "=r"(id_pfr1));
 	debug("id_pfr1: 0x%08x\n", id_pfr1);
@@ -913,6 +928,22 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_USB_GADGET
+/*
+ * misc_init_r() probes MUSB as a USB gadget.  Linux uses the controller as a
+ * host, so leave the hardware in reset at the handoff.
+ */
+void board_quiesce_devices(void)
+{
+	struct udevice *usb_dev;
+
+	/* A missing gadget is harmless; it may have failed to probe earlier. */
+	if (!uclass_first_device(UCLASS_USB_GADGET_GENERIC, &usb_dev) &&
+	    usb_dev)
+		device_remove(usb_dev, DM_REMOVE_NORMAL);
+}
+#endif
+
 int ft_board_setup(void *blob, bd_t *bd)
 {
 	int __maybe_unused r;
